      "message": "The issue this avoids is:\n```\nutil/ecst.c: In function \u0027main\u0027:\nutil/ecst.c:365:7: error: \u0027strncpy\u0027 output may be truncated copying 100 bytes from a string of length 9999 [-Werror\u003dstringop-truncation]\n  365 |       strncpy(hdr_args[arg_ind++],\n      |       ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  366 |        tmp_hdr_args[tmp_ind],\n      |        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  367 |        ARG_SIZE);\n      |        ~~~~~~~~~\n```\n\nwhich is bogus: gcc considers tmp_hdr_args[100][100] to be a single 10000 bytes string, and it\u0027s never used that way.",
